  "note": "Triennial election of 15 January 1923, the first after proportional representation was abolished; Portadown was divided into three wards (North 5 seats, South-East 4, South-West 6) by a Ministry of Home Affairs order of 31 October 1922 (Belfast Gazette, 10 November 1922). Messrs Campbell, Copeland, Corbett, Locke, Moffett, G. Johnston, W. J. Johnston and Mrs M'Cammon were the official nominees of the Labour Unionist Association; \"all the other candidates were Independent Unionists\". Counted 16 January. South-East Ward: Mrs Mary M'Cammon, second on the poll, was Portadown's first woman councillor; Robert Anderson, a member for 17 years, lost his seat."
